# cuts/v1.0.41/cut.env
# ============================================================================
# THE PINS FOR v1.0.41. Read by bin/rollforward_gate.sh --cut v1.0.41, by
# scripts/verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh, by scripts/resolve_cut_daemon_pin.sh,
# and by OS003 bin/cut.sh load_cut().
#
# THIS FILE IS THE AUTHORITATIVE HALF. OS003 carries a second cuts/v1.0.41/
# cut.env holding the operator's LOCAL PATHS. They are deliberately different
# documents. Do not merge them: vendoring OS003's copy here was tried and
# reverted because it carried operator working record, private box IPs and
# notarisation submission IDs into this PUBLIC repo.
#
# WHY v1.0.41 EXISTS: THE WIKI IMAGES SHIPPED A LIVE MEETING PASSCODE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CM044 #247 found that 17 of 928 Places pages carried a live meeting passcode
# IN THE PAGE TITLE, because a calendar's location field for a remote meeting
# IS the join URL. The wiki images pinned by v1.0.40 predate that fix.
#
# NO hold_ack WAS AVAILABLE FOR THIS DELTA, and that is the whole reason this
# is a rebuild rather than a sentence in scripts/wiki_hold_ack.tsv. Every prior
# ack in that file rests on its delta being docs-only, CI-only or test-only.
# This one carried fix() commits against customer-visible behaviour, and two of
# the changed files sit inside the site image's own COPY set.
#
# WHAT MOVED
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   wiki images   CM044 9af6ecaf -> 946a624 (tag v0.1.24)
#                 wiki-site      sha256:0df14b72...
#                 wiki-compiler  sha256:ab53c66a...
#   daemon        0.4.61 -> 0.4.62, hub-v0.4.62, built LOCALLY and signed
#   fallback      0.4.60 -> 0.4.61, with its own digest, per #583
#   installer     1.0.40 / 4000 -> 1.0.41 / 4100 across all three sources
#
# THE DAEMON WAS NOT TAG-PUSHED. A daemon tag push produces an UNSIGNED draft:
# release/sign-and-notarize.sh treats an empty identity as "skip signing" and
# exits 0, so the run is green and the binary is adhoc. Built with
# release/build-local.sh on the host with the keychain, then verified on the
# EXTRACTED artefact and again on the PUBLISHED bytes fetched anonymously.
#
# BOTH artefacts exist, which is what v1.0.38 was blocked on:
#   ostler-ai/ostler-releases   hub-v0.4.62  daemon,  Developer ID + notarised
#   ostler-ai/ostler-assistant  hub-v0.4.62  wrapper, ADHOC BY DESIGN
# Frontend parity proven from INSIDE the Mach-O, both directions, with the
# v0.4.61 wrapper as a negative control that correctly exits 1.
#
# freshness at the time this file was written:
#   fresh=18  held=4  exempt=5  stale/RED=0   GATE: GREEN
# ============================================================================

CUT_VERSION=1.0.41

# The daemon source commit. Dereferenced, never the annotated tag object.
DAEMON_COMMIT=9be3224c799a

# The tree whose install.sh ships. Compared BY BLOB by
# scripts/verify_cut_pin_is_current.sh, which fails closed -- ancestry proves
# ordering and says nothing about content, and cuts/v1.0.31 shipped the exact
# defect it existed to fix because its pin was an ancestor and stale.
# install.sh blob at this commit: 38175530c86775518e426b894b0838e523f954c3
# (identical at c5cd2f73, the re-pin commit; the version bump that followed
# touched only gui/, so the blob did not move.)
CM051=1db71eed27472e65bcd089caed274e4e57f6dba0
